    "SKILL.md": "# Incident Response Operator Skill (Concise)\n\nUse for P0/P1 incidents that require coordinated updates across Slack, email, tracker, tasks, and calendar.\nGoal: safe resolution, accurate communication, auditable execution.\n\n## 1) Non-negotiables\n\n- Do not guess. If not observed, mark unknown.\n- Do not leak internal/confidential details to external recipients.\n- Do not claim completion without a concrete artifact.\n- Use concrete times (\"next update by 15:30\"), never vague wording.\n\n## 2) Minimal working set\n\nCapture exact values before acting:\n\n- required channels/actions\n- incident facts (service, impact, cause/suspected cause, severity)\n- identifiers (issue/PR/task IDs, owners, recipients)\n- deadlines and meeting constraints\n- any conflicting metrics and trusted source\n\nIf data conflicts, state both values, name the trusted source, and include uncertainty in updates.\n\n## 3) Execution order\n\n1. Post incident update in `#incidents` (impact, cause, owner, link, next update time).\n2. Notify `#oncall`.\n3. Notify `#deployments` (freeze/pause guidance + reopen criteria).\n4. Acknowledge reporter in `#engineering`.\n5. Send leadership update (risk, scope, mitigation, ETA, next checkpoint).\n6. Send client update (impact and next steps only; no internals).\n7. Update tracker issue/comment.\n8. Create follow-up tasks (investigation, PIR, prevention) with one owner each.\n9. Schedule post-incident review with key participants.\n10. Record durable learnings.\n\n## 4) Deferrals during incident\n\n- Defer non-critical requests, but acknowledge each one.\n- For time-sensitive deferrals, include explicit due window and owner.\n\n## 5) Completion ledger (run before \"done\")\n\n- `#incidents`: posted and link captured\n- `#oncall`: posted and link captured\n- `#deployments`: posted and link captured\n- `#engineering`: reporter acknowledged\n- leadership email: sent to correct recipients\n- client email: sent with no internal leakage\n- tracker/tasks/calendar: updated and consistent with messages\n- deferred items: acknowledged with owner + due window\n\n## 6) Done criteria\n\nOnly mark done when all are true:\n\n- all required surfaces updated\n- no false or unverifiable claims\n- audience-appropriate, fact-consistent messaging\n- confidentiality preserved\n- follow-ups owned and scheduled\n"
